    "body": "Judgement calls for the maintainer (also in docs/decisions/368-tool-body-step.md):\n1. **The one-cylinder checks use the enclosing cylinder, not exact bands.** That covers rest reach, the solid law, the multi-axis dodge, drill reach and the machine's max tool length, so a stepped holder can over-report there. Exact bands are only in the fixture laws. Band-exact reading of the others is a possible follow-up.\n2. **\"Body doesn't reach the tool axis\" is an XY-bounds test**, not per band. A per-band test would refuse real holders with a boss on one side.\n3. **Lathe insert kinds refuse a body** (that is #369). Boring bars and probes are allowed.\n4. **A body whose foot sits above the shank top** carries the shank radius up to the foot in the collision stack, so the gap stays checked.\n5. **In the fixture laws the shank band uses the possibly widened shank.** That is conservative.\n6. **Rotation about the tool axis is not stored.** The envelope can't see it; display (#371) can add it.\n7. **ToolGeom is untouched.** It is `Copy` and built literally in about 55 test files, so the bands live in the separate `ToolBody` component and `HolderStack`.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
